WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.234
For this guided practice explain the three COUNT
patterns without running anything

00:00:04.261 --> 00:00:11.453
first COUNT star answers how many input rows are
present COUNT

00:00:11.466 --> 00:00:17.374
of a column answers how many non-null values that
expression contains COUNT

00:00:17.387 --> 00:00:23.031
DISTINCT answers how many unique non-null values
occur Try to create

00:00:23.057 --> 00:00:26.833
a small mental example with three rows including one
NULL and one

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:32.900
repeated value Predict what each COUNT would return
Then

00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:38.270
compare your explanation with the answer shown on
the slide This type

00:00:38.283 --> 00:00:42.760
of verbal reasoning is important If you can explain
the measure before

00:00:42.786 --> 00:00:45.681
you write the SQL you are less likely to choose a
count

00:00:45.707 --> 00:00:47.181
that answers the wrong question
